<title>FRANCE: Credit du Nord pays 77 mln Ffr in Laydernier buy.</title>
<headline>Credit du Nord pays 77 mln Ffr in Laydernier buy.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit du Nord will pay 77.28 million francs for 600,000 shares in Banque Laydernier, the bank owned by Credit Lyonnais, according to a finance ministry decree.</p>
<p>The sale was announced by the finance ministry on October 25 but with no price details.</p>
<p>The price was announced in a decree published on October 26.</p>
<p>Credit du Nord is controlled by Groupe Paribas.</p>
</text>
